{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pulls/512","id":4601644844,"node_id":"PR_kwDOP42Xbc8AAAABEkeHLA","html_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/512","diff_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/512.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/512.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/512","number":512,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(builder): bound AUDIO_UNIT sampling rates to the PP contract","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[A10] The builder accepted AUDIO_UNIT rate lists that the PP (protocol processor) cannot walk: a ninth advertised rate could be rejected by SET_SAMPLING_RATE. This change refuses lists longer than eight and duplicate entries, and detects drift between the hand-built pp_shadow rate list and its shipping configuration.\n\n## Status\n\nImplementation frozen at d81a302760b84f32d2aa019643f57682bb6e052c against dev ec34fcdee0ca9ffa63564a9af8ad70a3a618de29. All 40 static/builder and five full native commands passed at this source head against ec34fcde, with both validation clones integrity-verified. Full evidence: https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/478#issuecomment-5775843006 . Dev has since advanced to 88e9276b through #507; the new candidate bar remains pending. Exact-source-head trusted act, hosted checks and independent reviews follow publication.\n\nCloses #478\nRelates to #509\nPP contract: https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/89\n\nExecutor A156 (Codex); independent cleared-context reviewers R221 (internal Codex) and R222 (external Opus); manager A10.\n\n## Description\n\nA named maximum beside BASE_RATE_HZ mirrors PP memory-map rule L10. `_load_clocking` raises cause-specific ConfigError for a distinct ninth entry or any duplicate after integer conversion. Order, current-rate membership and omitted-list defaults are preserved.\n\nBuilder gate 36a exercises a legal eight-entry loader boundary, independent count and duplicate refusals, all five shipping images, and the existing literal pp_shadow AU_RATES_C values and declared length. Separate value, order, length, initializer and commented-declaration controls must fail. The pp_shadow image remains hand-built. The authoritative builder schema documents the bound.\n\nThe three-file issue delta is identical to A156's original 099e191137dd2797407fb8345a452bcc7a965608 after integrating dev. All five shipping config files and packed descriptor images are unchanged in the author's measured before/after comparison. No PP pin, donor implementation, runtime-rate policy or shipping-rate list is changed.\n\nAuthority: REQUIREMENTS.md REQ-VER-03/04; pinned PP `docs/architecture/07_memory_maps.md` section 3.1 L10; Milan v1.2 section 5.3.3.3; #478's public readiness decision and assignment.\n\n## How to reproduce\n\nFetch branch `478-audio-unit-rate-bound`, check out d81a302760b84f32d2aa019643f57682bb6e052c, and initialize `third_party/verilog-axis`, `protocol-processor` and `gptp-processor` at their gitlinks. The unused external submodule is not a validation dependency.\n\n## How to validate\n\nRun `python3 sw/builder/test_builder.py`, `python3 scripts/lint_rtl.py --check`, `python3 scripts/xvlog_gate.py --check`, the documentation gates and the complete CONTRIBUTING native bar: parent suite sweep, Yosys, both processor suites and behave. Gate 36a must reject each independent defect and accept its legal controls. Complete commands, exact heads, logs and disclosed skips are in the manager evidence comments.\n\nAuthor packet at its original head and first current-head manager evidence: https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/tree/b671cc625534af2d50f91f1fd0f8dac1ab49c991/review-evidence/478-r1 . Evidence branch never merges. The calibrated resource-report arm (builder gate 11) and field-campaign skips do not supply hardware evidence.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [x] Issue scope, decision and roles public; coherent implementation and focused author evidence.\n- [x] Input contract documented; shipping rates preserved.\n- [ ] Required complete native and exact-head hosted checks pass; trusted act replica passes.\n- [ ] Two independent positive reviews; all five reviewer-owned lenses clean; no review in flight.\n- [ ] Current-dev merge candidate validated; actual merge tree and post-merge containment verified.\n- [ ] Issue closed and Project Done after all completion checks.\n","created_at":"2026-09-22T11:46:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T11:48:09Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"9fea8a3cf41d3d996155aaca7a3aa1c167c057cf","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pulls/512/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pulls/512/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pulls/comments{/n